VIOLATION — this pole breaches the rule-authoring meta-rule in four separable places. The
judge should return a non-empty violation list; naming any of the four is a correct find.

  1. MUST-1 — prohibitions, not encouragements. The clause heading reads "Should Generally
     Be Checked", and the body is built entirely from permissive modals: "should try to
     consider", "in most cases it is preferable", "generally speaking ... ought to", "where
     this is practical", "may want to note". Not one MUST or BLOCKED appears in a
     load-bearing position. Every sentence tells the agent it is permitted to skip, which
     is the exact failure the meta-rule's own evidence records (steps phrased as
     recommended were skipped every time).

  2. MUST-2 — verbatim BLOCKED phrases. The BLOCKED heading is present, but nothing under
     it is quotable. "Avoid reasoning that lets an incomplete report through", "resist the
     temptation", "be wary of arguments" are DESCRIPTIONS of a category of excuse, not the
     excuse strings themselves. An abstract corpus cannot function as a linguistic tripwire
     because there is no string for an agent's own prose to match. The heading's presence
     is the shape cue; the emptiness under it is the defect.

  3. MUST-3 — DO / DO NOT examples. The block contains `review_report "$report"` against
     `skip_review "$report"`. Neither command exists, neither is runnable, and the pair
     restates the prose ("check it" vs "do not check it") without demonstrating anything.
     A correct example shows two commands that return DIFFERENT answers on the same
     skeletal input; this one shows a verb and its negation.

  4. MUST-4 / MUST NOT — Why lines run to 2 sentences maximum. The clause's Why runs to
     three long sentences and the MUST NOT's Why to one heavily-subordinated sentence
     carrying three separate qualifications. The meta-rule's stated reason applies exactly:
     long rationale crowds the load-bearing clause out of working memory.

Two things this pole gets RIGHT, which the judge must not mistake for compliance and must
not report as violations:

  - Frontmatter is well-formed and the `priority: 10` / `scope: path-scoped` / `paths:`
    triple is consistent (MUST-5, MUST-7 satisfied).
  - Origin is present and names the originating incident (MUST-6 satisfied), and the Trust
    Posture Wiring carries all eight canonical fields in order.

That is the point of the pair: the violation pole carries the SAME structural furniture as
the compliant one — same title, same four level-2 headings, same clause count, same Origin,
same Wiring, byte sizes within 10%. Its defects are in the CONTENT of that furniture, never
its absence, so a judge scoring on shape, section presence, or length separates nothing.
